{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Then she said.</b> What is 'then she said'? At first, when she saw the angel swallowing him up to the circumcision, she did not know whether it was because of delaying his son's circumcision or because of his own circumcision — for he had relations with her and she was not fitting for him. And even so, she cut off her son's foreskin and touched it to his feet and said, 'For you are a bridegroom of blood' — perhaps it is on his account that you are being punished; leave him alone. 'Then she said, a bridegroom of blood for circumcisions' — now I know with certainty that you are not being punished except because of the delay of your son's circumcision. From Rabbi Elijah Cohen, of blessed memory."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:41.760204004Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}